{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/divisions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/divisions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"divisions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","text":"MXLDivisions"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"code":"divisions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Used the same way as the divisions attribute of the sound element, to indicate the number of divisions per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quarter note for playback when this barline contains a segno or coda child element.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"divisions","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"divisions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","text":"MXLDivisions"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV9divisionsAA12MXLDivisionsVSgvp","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/divisions":{"title":"divisions","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/divisions","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Used the same way as the divisions attribute of the sound element, to indicate the number of divisions per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quarter note for playback when this barline contains a segno or coda child element.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"divisions"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDivisionsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/divisions"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDivisions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDivisions","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDivisions","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The divisions type is used to express values in terms of the musical divisions defined by the divisions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. It is preferred that these be integer values both for MIDI interoperability and to avoid roundoff"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"errors."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldivisions","title":"MXLDivisions"}}}